{title: The Water Is Wide}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
The [C]water is [F]wide, I [C]cannot get [Am]o'er,
And [Dm]neither [G7]have I [C]wings to [G7]fly.
Give [C]me a [F]boat that can [C]carry [Am]two,
And [F]both shall [G7]row, my love and [C]I.

{c: Verse 2}
There [C]is a [F]ship and [C]she sails the [Am]sea,
She's [Dm]loaded [G7]deep as [C]deep can [G7]be.
But [C]not so [F]deep as the [C]love I'm [Am]in,
I [F]know not [G7]how I sink or [C]swim.
